    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.maximal_matching - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.maximal_matching.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.maximal_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find a maximal matching in the graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.maximal_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find a maximal matching in the graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.maximal_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find a maximal matching in the graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind a maximal matching in the graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L76378-L76466){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.maximal_matching()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Maximal matching](../assets/graphs/maximal-matching.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A five-node graph: a triangle 2, 3, 5 with pendant nodes 1 and 4. The greedy maximal matching takes edge 2–3 first (accent); every other edge touches 2 or 3, so nothing more can be added, even though the larger matching 1–2, 3–4 exists. The card shows the returned edge id 1, the pair 2–3, and size 1.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA maximal matching is a matching (set of edges with no shared endpoints) that cannot be\nextended by adding any other edge. Uses a greedy algorithm that scans edges in creation\n(edge ID) order, so the result is deterministic for a given graph but can change if the\nsame edges are added in a different order.\n\nNote that a maximal matching is not necessarily a maximum matching (largest possible). For\nweighted graphs, use `maximum_weight_matching()`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   List of edge IDs forming a maximal matching.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nRuns a greedy scan of the edge list in $O(E)$: each edge whose endpoints are both\nstill unmatched joins the matching and marks them off. The result is *maximal* in\nthe inclusion-ordering sense (no further edge can be added without a conflict) but\nnot necessarily *maximum*: a matching that ties up the wrong endpoints first can\nleave more edges dangling than an optimal one would. For maximum cardinality\nmatching on general graphs, Edmonds' blossom algorithm runs in $O(V \\cdot E)$ but\nis far more elaborate; for bipartite inputs, Hopcroft-Karp's $O(E \\sqrt{V})$ is\nthe workhorse. When edge weights matter, `maximum_weight_matching()` handles the\nobjective-aware variant.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~maximum_weight_matching`) \n\n:   The largest matching, or the heaviest.\n\n[](`~is_maximal_matching`) \n\n:   Check that no edge can be added to a matching.\n\n[](`~edge_coloring`) \n\n:   Split all the edges into matchings.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe greedy matching takes the edges in the order they were added, skipping any that\ntouch a node already matched. In this path, it takes the first edge, then the third:\n\n::: {#91594e17 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\nlabel = path.get_label_from_id\n[\n    [label(n) for n in path.get_node_ids_by_edge_id(e)]\n    for e in path.maximal_matching()\n]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['A', 'B'], ['C', 'D']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nAdded in another order, the middle edge comes first and blocks both of the others:\n\n::: {#788c7a7b .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"B\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"B\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\nlen(path.maximal_matching())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n1\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Two left without a partner\n\n`friends()` links 24 members of two clubs in a made-up town, a chess club and a climbing\nclub, who are friends. Going through the friendships in order, the greedy matching\nforms 11 pairs, and Lou and Zane, who aren't friends, are left over. A maximum matching\npairs all 24:\n\n::: {#a503a83f .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends = ec.friends()\ngreedy = friends.maximal_matching()\n\npaired = {n for e in greedy for n in friends.get_node_ids_by_edge_id(e)}\nlabel = friends.get_label_from_id\nleft = [label(n) for n in friends.get_node_ids() if n not in paired]\n\nlen(greedy), left, len(friends.maximum_weight_matching())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(11, ['Lou', 'Zane'], 12)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#6150a831 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends.plot(\n    highlight={\"accent\": left}, highlight_edges={\"soft\": greedy},\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=2,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-9f8a22df:#efc5b7;--ect-6c2f7015:#a78980;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-9f8a22df:#4c2e23;--ect-6c2f7015:#352018;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-9f8a22df:#efc5b7;--ect-6c2f7015:#a78980;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-9f8a22df:#4c2e23;--ect-6c2f7015:#352018;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"5.6 14.0 688.8 492.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=